A||||3||loafer87gt||Performance questions...||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||07-14-2000||02:21 PM||||Hey guys,<P>I got my Fiero towed to my mechanic yesterday and it turns out the sick sounding noise my car is making is a turned bearing, and the crankshaft is scarred because of it. Instead of trying to rebuild the engine, I am just going to buy an 3.0 V6 from RS motorsports. This engine has the larger throttle body, a more aggressive cam, 1.6 roller rockers,and ported heads. I am wondering what other mods I should do at the same time. What is a good low cost exhaust system? From what I've heard, the flow master from Chris West is a good choice, but does include anmy of the piping, or is it just the muffler? Also, I remember seeing on somebodies site a cold air induction kit, it had a conical air filter attachment and got rid of the stock air canister, can anyone remember the name of the guy? Anyways, I'm pretty excited, I've been looking forward to doing the engine on my car for some now, and I think this combo should be a lot more responsive than the old 2.8. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Taijiguy||07-14-2000||02:24 PM||||Why not just go with a 3.4? Just as easy as any other changeover you could make.<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||07-14-2000||02:44 PM||||Some where on this forum I saw the price of the K&N induction system was $350. <A HREF="http://www.fieronl/forum2/HTML/004726.html" TARGET=_blank>www.fieronl/forum2/HTML/004726.html</A>  Hedders are a good option, cause you original exhaust manifold may be cracked.  Once they get the old engine out you'll be able to see all.<P>You have so many choices at this point on engine swaps and build ups.  Flow master exhaust or Borla exhaust, free flow cat, hedders.  While the engine is out, now is the time to do the mods, so much easier to do.  You know how much you can spend. Hedders $650-850 (powder coated?) Stainless steel exhaust $250-500.  Cat $50-100.  So many things and so much money.<p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 07-14-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000003||chris west||07-14-2000||08:31 PM||||Hi guys this is Will here at West Coast Fiero and i would have to go with the 3.4 asw well. In gett9ing to ur question about piping with that muffler you dont need any new pipe becuse it well mount up to ur stock pipe. We do have a complet system headers cat and muffler also we have a new cold air induction system for only $250 and it is much better that anyothers on the market today just some thoughts if u would like to check us out our site is <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A>  or u can call at 310 305 4111 thanks||||reg||1
